A||||1||zeusrekning||Bad news update on 455||||1||
Z||000000||zeusrekning||08-15-2000||08:05 PM||||I got the 455 for $450. It was locked down it had gotten rain in the right bank. But worse of all the shorted me 55 cubic inches. It is a 400. It had 4x heads. 2.11 And 1.66 valves. I called the guy i bought it from and told him what i found out and he said he would find a replacement.. What heads should i look for? Oh yeah the combustion chamber on those heads were 114 cc.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-16-2000||02:42 PM||||Before you make that trip home with the next motor, look at the side of the block in front of the starter mount. It should say "455". Pontiac did us all a favor buy actually casting the displacement into all the blocks from the late 60's until they quit making them.<P>As far as heads, the 114cc's seem a little large. Although the 455 doesn't need (or really like) high compression to make torque, it will help it to rev faster if the compresion is at least 8.5-9.0. So, I would guess something in the mid 90's cc range would be better.<P>Again, I encourage you to try <A HREF="http://www.classicalpontiac.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classicalpontiac.com</A>  and post some questions there. You'll get some great info from some really nice guys.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
